/**
 * JWT Refresh Token Middleware for Hono.
 *
 * Verifies an access token from the `Authorization` header. If the access token
 * is valid, sets `jwtPayload` and proceeds. If the access token is expired but a
 * valid refresh token is present in a cookie, calls `onRefresh` to mint a new
 * access token, sets it in a response header, and proceeds. Otherwise responds
 * with `401 Unauthorized`.
 *
 * @param {object} options - The options for the JWT refresh middleware.
 * @param {SignatureKey} options.secret - The secret used to verify the access token.
 * @param {SignatureAlgorithm} options.alg - The signature algorithm used for both tokens.
 * @param {SignatureKey} [options.refreshSecret] - The secret used to verify the refresh token. Defaults to `secret`.
 * @param {string} [options.refreshCookie='refresh_token'] - The cookie name to read the refresh token from.
 * @param {string} [options.headerName='Authorization'] - The header name to read the access token from.
 * @param {string} [options.responseHeader='X-Access-Token'] - The response header to set the new access token on after a refresh.
 * @param {VerifyOptions} [options.verification] - Additional options for JWT payload verification.
 * @param {(payload: unknown) => Promise<string>} options.onRefresh - Callback invoked with the refresh token payload that must return a new access token.
 * @returns {MiddlewareHandler} The middleware handler function.
